WEBVTT

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.050
Yunocchi!

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.550
Are you up yet?

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.800
Yeah!

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.010
Morning, Miya-chan.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.490
Morning, Yunocchi.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.060
Look at that!

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.590
Wow!

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.570
It looks like it was made overnight.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.130
That's amazing!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:51.820
I know, right?

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.830
Good morning!

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.870
Yuno-san, Miyako-san, good morning.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.210
Good morning!

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.460
Morning!

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.790
I'm glad that the rain stopped.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.430
Yeah!

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.340
I got to see a marvel of nature too!

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.090
Yeah!

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.190
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.190
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.530
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.530
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.450
When fatigue strikes

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.450
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.070
My imagination runs wild

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.070
atama ga danshingu

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.530
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.530
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.370
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.370
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.000
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.000
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.630
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.630
aozora peintingu

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.670
Where should we go?

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.670
doko ikou

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.250
Let's stay here

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.250
koko ni iyou

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.250
What's that?

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.250
sore wa nani

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.840
I wanna try that!

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.840
are yaritai

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.430
Let's make this moment count

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.430
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:58.810
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:58.810
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.480
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.480
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.940
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.940
nonbiri na everyday

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.560
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.560
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.400
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.400
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.990
So when your heart races in excitement

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.990
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.700
Just draw a sun at the top

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.700
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.830
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.830
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.160
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.160
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.550
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.550
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.090
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.090
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.850
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.850
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.010
October 11th,
October 30th,
Terror! Preparing for
the Yamabuki Festival

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.020
For our homeroom activity today,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.160
we're going to decide what to do as a class for this year's Yamabuki festival.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.160
If you have <i>any</i> suggestions, please raise your hand.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:55.910
Me!

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.140
Yes, Sensei?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.290
What about a costume parade?

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.040
Costume parade...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.540
Any other ideas?

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.290
Me!

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.340
What about a maid café?

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.940
I think we have enough ideas now, so let's move onto the vote.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.760
We'll be handing out the ballot slips—

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:17.350
Wait!

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.470
Let's vote with a show of hands! I'll count!

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:25.220
Have you decided on what you're voting for, everyone?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.110
Now, close your eyes!

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:34.180
If you want to vote for the first choice, the costume parade, then please raise your hand now.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:34.860
I promise

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.220
to keep your votes a secret.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.870
Then why do I still feel like I'm under pressure?

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:41.620
Okay!

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:46.740
We're going to make a haunted house for this year's Yamabuki festival.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.380
Yay!

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.700
A haunted house, huh?

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.680
I definitely wouldn't want to walk through one,
but <i>making</i> a haunted house sounds kind of fun.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.820
What do you want to be, Yunocchi?

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.770
You mean like, what kind of ghost?

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.430
Let me think.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.100
A zashiki-warashi?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.190
That doesn't sound too scary.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.190
Yuno-san!

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:09.940
Mami-chan!

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.280
You're doing a great job on the festival committee!

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:17.980
Could you do a huge favor for the girl in charge of the pamphlets?

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.040
She wanted a little blurb from the cover artist.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.060
Tell us how you feel about the Yamabuki Festival

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:27.370
and being chosen for the pamphlet cover.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.940
Is two pages long enough?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.880
Eight hundred characters?! That's way too much!

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.390
I hear your class is doing a haunted house.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:45.200
Yeah, we are!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.360
We're only responsible for the class attraction this year,

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.880
so it shouldn't be as much work.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.600
Second-years don't need a piece for the personal exhibits, do they?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.150
We do.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:57.360
The covers we drew for the pamphlet competition will be put on exhibit.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.300
Oh yeah, that's what the second-years do!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.600
I see!

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.700
A haunted house, huh?

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.320
How about your class, Sae-san, Hiro-san?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.800
We'll have udon.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.830
Wow!

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.980
Like udon art?

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.840
We're not talking about the exhibit!

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.700
What's your class doing, Nazuna-chan?

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.340
Oh, we're doing a balloon room.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.180
A balloon room?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.980
We're going to set off part of the classroom

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.680
with dividing walls and fill it up with balloons!

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.680
Wow! That sounds fun!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.440
You'll need a lot of balloons, though!

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.080
Yeah!

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.680
We put in a big order already, actually!

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.440
Balloons and...

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.110
handheld oxygen cans!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.500
You think you can inflate all of them by yourselves?

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.530
What's your class doing, Norisuke-san?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:45.540
We're putting on a performance of <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.400
D-Don't tell me you're going to be Juliet!

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.860
Of course not!

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.790
I'm in charge of props.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.540
The actors for Romeo and Juliet are both guys!

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.380
They're adding their own spice to it.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.580
Romeo's family, the House of Montague,

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.940
will be a farmer family that raises "Monta cows," for instance.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.180
That might as well be a different play, then.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.760
How do we make it scary?

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.570
It's our chance to show off our art skills, so we shouldn't cut any corners.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:24.120
We can't even make the blood red.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.100
We have to mix in some green to make it more realistic.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.100
But more realistic isn't always better, is it?

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.460
I guess not.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.340
I wonder if there's any way to make this scarier.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.090
Oh!

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:42.100
I heard it feels scarier if the ground beneath your feet is unstable.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.840
Oh, definitely!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.930
It certainly would be frightening if there was no light and the floor wasn't stable.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.800
But making it <i>too</i> unstable might end up being a safety hazard.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.770
Yeah, probably.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.650
Miya-chan, are you okay?

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.780
I'm fine.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.280
Your fingers!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.540
Okay, you're all better now.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.080
It's just a sprain, but you have to keep them bandaged for a week.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.500
A week...

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.920
That means I'll still have it on when the festival comes around.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.920
I know it's hard, but it'll only get worse if you don't take care of it now.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.080
Be careful not to strain it too much.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.660
Understood! Thank you very much.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.600
Thank you.

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.850
Miya-chan, let me know if there's anything I can help with, okay?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.900
Thanks, Yunocchi!

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.400
Actually, I need some help right now.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.380
Can you help me get changed?

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.620
My back feels wet.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.120
All right, I'm done!

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:53.660
<i>"My cover was inspired by last year's Yamabuki Festival.</i>

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.320
<i>I made sure to fill it with all my fun memories."</i>

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.840
Yunocchi, where's the face towel?

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:03.300
Oh, sorry, I'll get you one!

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:09.560
<i>"So I'm really happy that my cover design was chosen."</i>

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:14.100
<i>"I hope we have loads of fun at this year's Yamabuki Festival!"</i>

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.900
Sorry I'm such a bother.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.600
I can't believe it. My painting is on the cover!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.760
Wow!

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.180
Miya-chan, can you wait here for a minute?

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:52.010
Huh? Sure, I guess!

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:02.040
She could just ask for multiple copies.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.800
Mami-chan, good morning!

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.200
Morning!

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.450
Yuno-san, Miya-chan, good morning.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.500
Are your fingers all right?

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.460
Yeah, thanks.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.250
Sorry I couldn't help.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.040
Yuno-san, Miyako-san, do you want to get dressed up right now?

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.500
Sure!

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.820
Can we walk around the festival in the morning?

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:28.050
Sure, as long as you're not on-duty.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.440
Miya-chan, since you can't use your right hand,

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.980
let me handle things today.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:35.100
Thanks.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.500
Where do you wanna go?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.640
Should we go see Sae-san's class?

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.600
Yeah!

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.230
Sae-san! Hiro-san!

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.990
Your udon café uniforms are really well-done.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.660
Jeez, you scared us.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.000
Y-You almost gave me a heart attack.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:02.780
Sae-san, Hiro-san, can we take a picture?

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.630
Oh, sure.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.820
Thanks for coming, by the way.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.180
May I take your order?

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.920
Let's see... I'll have the udon café combo!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.390
Me too.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.140
Miya-chan!

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:20.190
I'll help you eat your udon, okay?

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.020
Thanks, but I can take care of myself.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:28.530
You're chugging it?!

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.680
Heart-shaped balloon...

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:39.640
Found it!

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:41.200
Oh, this is a rabbit.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.200
Heart, heart...

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.740
Wow, I found it!

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.460
Yunocchi, I found it!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.420
Really?

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.440
There's something written on it.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.420
It says...

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:51.400
"Good fortune."

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:56.180
So it's not one of those "you'll live happily ever after if you find it" things.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.440
Juliet-san really <i>is</i> a boy!

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.190
Juliet!

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:08.240
Come raise Monta cows with me!

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.040
I can't, Romeo!

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.380
Once I was kicked back 30 meters by a fighting bull,

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.540
and now I can't stand cows!

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.420
Juliet, don't worry!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.830
You'll get used to them! Look!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:23.920
Moo.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:25.170
No!

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:28.730
Hey, Norippe-san isn't performing in this play, is she?

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.420
Yeah, she said she's handling the props, so she probably isn't performing.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:36.680
You can do it! Overcome your trauma, Juliet!

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.930
Moo. Moo. Moo.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.930
Stand up, Juliet!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:42.500
She <i>is</i> performing!

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.520
You're right!

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.770
Maybe they didn't have enough people.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.020
<i>I was supposed to stay behind the scenes.</i>

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.020
Man...

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:50.560
Nori-chan cried.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.640
She sure did!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.660
It was definitely a human cry.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.780
Human?

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.040
Miya-chan!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.160
Here you go!

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.790
It's so good!

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.700
I just can't eat yakisoba with my broken fingers.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.660
Thanks.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.700
No problem.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.300
The stands have great food!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:18.930
Here, Miya-chan!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.040
Chocolate banana and takoyaki!

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:21.920
Open up!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.180
Oh, more food!

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.760
<i>Sorry, Miya-chan.</i>

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:34.320
<i>I'm getting the same feeling as when I want to feed more paper into the shredder.</i>

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.020
What?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:43.760
Oh!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.520
Arisawa-san!

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.210
Oh, Yuno-san!

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.580
How are you?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.860
You came after all!

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.060
Of course I did!

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.960
I missed Yamabuki so much!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.620
Oh, this is my friend from college.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:56.470
Hello!

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.720
Hello! Nice to meet you.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.560
We're about to get lunch.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.360
Would you like to join us?

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:07.100
Oh, sorry, but we just had lunch.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:10.500
Our shift's coming up too, so we need to head back.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.810
I see. Oh well.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.940
We'll come see you after lunch then!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.240
Okay! We'll be waiting!

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.240
So many great pieces this year!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.000
Oh!

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.500
Can I have one chocolate banana, please?

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:35.260
I got carried away and bought too many!

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.130
We're back!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.640
Our turn's coming up, right?

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.140
Welcome back!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.600
Have fun!

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.270
Got it!

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:52.560
This is Yuno's class's haunted house.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.520
I hear people screaming.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.780
I can tell this is going to be scary!

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:58.940
Wow!

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:02.380
They painted a board with gouache paint for this set.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.910
They put in a lot of effort.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:07.300
H-How can you be so calm?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.900
You guys are the scary ones.

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:19.840
Let's see...

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:24.500
"For your safety, please don't run inside the haunted house."

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.820
It's like the real thing.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.680
I-I hear strange voices!

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.480
Nazuna, let go of me.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:34.480
I can't stand them!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.320
Don't do that!

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.460
Sorry!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.970
Did you hear more voices?

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.220
Th-That almost got me.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.730
Someone has to put their hand in there and take out the talisman.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.680
I can't do it!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.940
Me neither.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:15.680
Nori-chan, sorry!

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.980
Fine, fine.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.570
<i>I don't like this.</i>

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.450
Is this it?

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.620
Don't run!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.640
This hand is obviously fake!

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.630
Jeez, give me a break!

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.710
Did you get the talisman?

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:42.470
Yep!

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.850
Thank you, Nori-chan!

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:49.980
I'm amazed that it takes so long to walk around a simple classroom.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.220
I know, right?

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.900
Isn't that the exit?

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.180
You're right!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.700
But where are Yuno-san and Miyako-san?

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.720
Oh, you made it!

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:06.530
Yuno!

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.340
You're the receptionist?

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:10.160
It was so scary!

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:14.000
Now, please place your talisman here.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:23.900
This is the class that everyone said was really scary, right?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.760
Yeah, I'm stoked!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:28.400
I heard it's pretty elaborate and spooky!

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.510
Really?

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.140
It's a huge hit!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.390
Yay!

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.180
Wow!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.620
I'm so glad.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.240
Thanks to the screams leaking out into the hallway

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.840
and the word of mouth of the people who made it through.

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:44.280
Yeah, I hear them!

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.980
That was terrifying!

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.780
It sure was!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.660
Mom? Dad?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.910
Oh, Yuno!

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.380
You found us!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.520
Huh? Why are you here?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:59.750
To check out your pamphlet, of course!

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:04.100
We didn't want to trouble you, so we didn't tell you.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:08.260
You should show your parents around.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.260
Huh? Yeah.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.420
But today we need to...

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.620
There! You're all ready to advertise!

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.100
<i>That's so embarrassing!</i>

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.570
Now a commemorative photo!

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:29.560
Okay, line up.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.880
Miya-chan, this is embarrassing.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.790
Just go!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.040
The actual piece has some real impact!

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.600
We'll have to frame it up when you get it back.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:42.820
Yep!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:44.220
Let's get one ready.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:47.680
It has to be a great frame that matches the piece!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.820
All right! I'll order a custom one!

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:52.550
Dad, this is embarrassing.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.560
This is so hard to eat.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:59.440
Huh? Is it that hard to eat?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.860
Your dad's just being clumsy.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.700
I'm sexy Momotarou...

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.200
Yoshinoya!

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.080
Dear visitors!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.460
I'm holding a one-man parade,

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:21.830
so make sure to watch!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:24.750
Yoshinoya-sensei?!

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:31.010
Out of my way!

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.160
That last one was a little too freaky.

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:39.470
Yamabuki students never disappoint.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:43.260
Now I know where all your creative ideas come from.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.360
You do?

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.610
I wonder where Yuno-san is.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.860
I haven't seen her once.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:52.860
We'll be heading home, then.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.260
You're not going to stay?

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.740
No. We'll call you later.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.370
Okay!

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.500
Thanks for coming, Mom and Dad!

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:02.140
Of course!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.940
Give our regards to Miya-chan too.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:04.800
I will!

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:09.200
Maybe we can get more pamphlets at the information desk on our way out.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.260
Do you think we should get back in line a few times?

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:23.220
<i>I wonder if Arisawa-san dropped by already.</i>

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.960
The time is 4:50.

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.780
Where did the time go?!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:31.020
Dear visitors, I hope you have enjoyed your visit.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:36.020
Yamabuki students, please start cleaning up.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:41.410
As a surprise, the night festival is beginning at 5:30.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:45.940
There will be a folk dance in the schoolyard, so please join us.

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:47.670
I gotta hurry!

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.420
It's Arisawa-san!

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:54.220
<i>Yuno-san, good work today!</i>

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:56.320
<i>I love the pamphlet cover!</i>

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.460
<i>My friend said it's wonderful too.</i>

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.580
<i>Your haunted house was super scary!</i>

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:04.200
<i>We'll be heading back now.</i>

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.400
<i>See you next time!</i>

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:10.340
<i>Arisa-san, thank you for coming today!</i>

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:13.340
<i>Please give my regards to your friend.</i>

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:14.980
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:19.450
<i>I want to meet up with Miya-chan, but she doesn't have a cell phone.</i>

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.700
<i>We should have agreed on a place to meet beforehand.</i>

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.710
<i>There was a sign on my back!</i>

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.240
I don't think so.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:59.740
Thanks for everything you've done today, Yunocchi.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:04.500
Huh? I couldn't be with you as much as I should've, though.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.750
Don't be so modest.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.320
With you around, I couldn't have felt more at ease.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.220
Thank you.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.000
Sure.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:10.750
Oh!

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:13.300
You took off your bandage, didn't you?

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.840
Is the pain gone?

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:15.760
Nah.

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:18.510
It still hurts to hold hands, so I got a replacement.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.780
Today was a busy day!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:39.900
Yamabuki's festival was so much fun!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.530
I walked around so much that I feel tired now.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.540
S-Spider!

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.800
I gotta wash it away!

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:58.970
But wait, they say it's good to have house spiders around.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.500
I guess it's like a zashiki-warashi.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:13.210
Hidamari personality test, begin!

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:15.370
You come to a fork in the road. Which path do you take?

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:15.890
Hm...

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:16.350
Up!

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:18.230
And you meet somebody there.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:19.190
The principal!

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:21.230
Tell me your two favorite numbers.

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:23.570
Let's see... 7 and 24.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:26.650
You'll fall in love with the principal, get married with him at 24,

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:28.430
and have seven children!

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:29.330
What?!

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:30.850
Did someone say my name?

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:35.290
Next time: "November 10th, Giving Back a Smile."

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:38.690
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments, so come visit us!
